From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <fardjad.davari2@jumbo.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 04:11:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add typed OpenRouter EU provider

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: typed EU deployment identity, auth, caches, and pricing
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-provider
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1002-personal-provider-family-allowlist.patch

Patch intent:
Add OpenRouter EU as a first-class typed deployment with an EU endpoint,
isolated credentials and caches, autocomplete, TUI visibility, and pricing
lookup that uses EU catalog and endpoint cache rates.

Why it exists:
Lets users route through a European OpenRouter endpoint with separate API keys
and cache namespaces. Non-goal is changing the standard OpenRouter provider or
its credentials.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-provider-core/src/lib.rs adds RuntimeKey::OpenRouterEu,
OpenRouterDeploymentId::Eu, ModelRouteApiMethod::OpenRouterEu, and their
mappings to ProviderFamily::OpenRouterEu from the allowlist patch.
crates/jcode-provider-openrouter-runtime/src/lib.rs adds the EU runtime factory.
crates/jcode-provider-openrouter/src/lib.rs adds namespace-specific cache functions.
crates/jcode-provider-metadata/src/catalog.rs adds the EU login provider entry.
crates/jcode-base/src/provider/selection.rs, activation.rs, mod.rs wire EU selection.
src/cli/login.rs and provider_init.rs add EU login and init flows.
crates/jcode-tui/ adds EU auth, header, onboarding, and model suggestions.

Update guidance:
Keep openrouter and openrouter-eu as separate families. Preserve EU endpoint,
cache namespace, and credential isolation. Keep the EU runtime reusing the
standard OpenRouter runtime implementation with only deployment-specific
overrides.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-provider-openrouter-runtime eu_openrouter --lib
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-provider-core runtime_key_ --lib
